survey-recorded interactions repeated at each wave are a legitimate shape
that a heuristic would misread:
\itemize{
\item the \strong{style} (\code{layers}): the process the layer records.
\code{"mutually_exclusive"} is a binary tie that is created and dissolved,
\code{"count"} is one monotone process of repeated events, and \code{"none"} is a
valued layer with no process, typically a covariate.
\item the \strong{form} (\code{form}): what a value at a wave means. \code{"states"} (the
default) is the level at the wave, \code{"per_wave"} is the amount since the
previous wave, and \code{"changes"} means the rows already are a change-list
in the layer's \code{update} semantics.
